-- title:
--   Monodromy bound for ℓ-power torsion on J₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \geq 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ given by `hK` as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-function field of $X_1(Mp)$ inside Laurent series over $L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly ($A \to L \to K$ a scalar tower), and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). All statements below concern the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, which is assumed proper.
--
--   Special-fibre geometry. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra, and let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral. Closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ over $k$ embed $C_1, C_2$ into the base change of the two-chart model to $k$; the hypothesis `hcover` asserts that every point of that base change lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred` asserts that the scheme-theoretic intersection `pullback i₁.1 i₂.1` is reduced, and `hn`, `hn0` fix its cardinality to be $n > 0$.
--
--   Relative Picard data. A section $\varepsilon$ of the model over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ is given, together with sections $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ of $c_1, c_2$ and the compatibility `hε₁`, namely that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$. Let $D$ be a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation for the model over $A$ (a scheme with a structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section), assumed via `hrep` to represent the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles that are fibrewise algebraically equivalent to zero, in the sense of `RepresentsRelSubPic`: a Poincaré rigidified bundle on $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ satisfying the condition, universal for that condition, and trivial along the zero section. The structure morphism of $D$ is assumed smooth (`hsm`) and separated (`hsep`). The corresponding representability after base change to $k$ is `hreps`, and `hPk` provides an isomorphism of the resulting Poincaré bundle with the base change of the Poincaré bundle of $D$; $D_1, D_2$ are designations for $c_1, c_2$ with representability `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`. A morphism $\nu_2$ over $k$ from the base change of $D$ to $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ is given, and `hν₂` asserts that for every $k$-scheme $T$ and every $T$-point $a$ of the base change of $D$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of $D_2$ along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification, along the section induced by $\varepsilon_2$, of the restriction along `curveChange i₂.1` of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` along $a$; thus $\nu_2$ realises restriction of line bundles to the component $C_2$.
--
--   Generic fibre. With $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` an $A$-algebra and an $L$-algebra compatibly, $M_\eta$ is a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) (a proper smooth integral curve with its function field identified with that field and a bijection between closed points and places), and $e_\eta$ is an isomorphism of $M_\eta.C$ with the generic fibre of the model, compatible with the structure morphisms (`heη`). The chart hypotheses `Mη_chart_nonempty` and `hMηpin` state that the preimage in $M_\eta.C$ of the finite chart is nonempty and that for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) the germ at the generic point of the function pulled back along $e_\eta$ followed by the projection to the model corresponds, under $M_\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, to the Laurent series obtained from $a \in K \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ by applying [`ModularCurve.coeffMap`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) to $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The hypothesis `hgal` is Galois equivariance of the point–place dictionary: for every $g \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$, if $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, then $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x' = \mathrm{arithmeticGalois}(g) \cdot M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x$.
--
--   Special-fibre group dictionary. $G$ is a [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9): abelian groups $J_{0s}$, $J_I$, $J_E$, a subgroup $\mathrm{torus} \leq J_{0s}$ and a surjective homomorphism $\mathrm{proj} : J_{0s} \to J_I \times J_E$ with kernel exactly $\mathrm{torus}$. Bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` identify $J_{0s}, J_I, J_E$ with the $k$-points of the base change of $D$ and of $D_1, D_2$ respectively; `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` assert that each dictionary is additive, the Poincaré pullback at $a+b$ being isomorphic to the tensor product of those at $a$ and $b$; `hproj` asserts that for $x \in J_{0s}$ the first component of $\mathrm{proj}\,x$ corresponds to `pts x` followed by the classifying morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom` attached to $i_1$, and the second component to `pts x` followed by $\nu_2$. The components are pinned to Igusa curves: for an integral weight-one form $w$ on $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ (a weight-one modular form together with an integral $q$-expansion whose reduction in $k$ is nonzero), curve models $\mathrm{Mdl}_1, \mathrm{Mdl}_2$ of [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) are given with isomorphisms $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$, $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he₁`, `he₂`).
--
--   Abel–Jacobi dictionary over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. A bijection `gpts` identifies $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp) = \mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, \mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp))$ with the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$, and `hgadd` asserts that it is additive for the relative group law supplied by `hrep`. The block `hDL`, `ajL`, `kL`, `ajbar`, `εbar`, `hPL`, `hajLε`, `hajL`, `hkL₁`, `hkL₂`, `hajbar`, `hajbar_over`, `hεbar`, `hεbar_aj`, `hpts_aj` (summarised here) provides: representability after base change to $L$ with a Poincaré comparison isomorphism; a morphism $\mathrm{ajL}$ from the $L$-fibre of the curve to the $L$-base change of $D$ which sends the section induced by $\varepsilon$ to the zero section and which, for every field $K'$ and every $K'$-point $x$ over $\operatorname{Spec} L$, pulls the Poincaré bundle back to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the $\varepsilon$-point, i.e. $\mathrm{ajL}$ is the Abel–Jacobi map $x \mapsto [x - \varepsilon]$; a morphism $\mathrm{kL}$ from the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-fibre to the $L$-fibre compatible with both projections; the composite $\mathrm{ajbar} = e_\eta \mathbin{;} \mathrm{kL} \mathbin{;} \mathrm{ajL} \mathbin{;} \mathrm{pullback.fst}$ lying over the structure morphism of $M_\eta$; a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\overline{\varepsilon}$ of $M_\eta.C$ inducing $\varepsilon$ and sent by $\mathrm{ajbar}$ to the zero section; and the compatibility `hpts_aj` stating that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x$ and $s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ the $\varepsilon$-point there is a degree-zero divisor $Dv$ equal to $[\,\mathrm{place}(x)\,] - [\,\mathrm{place}(s)\,]$ with `gpts (Pic0.mk Dv)` equal to $x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajbar}$.
--
--   Inertia data. $\mathrm{Pl}$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its nonunits, $\rho : A \to \mathrm{Pl}$ a ring homomorphism inducing $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $\pi_k : \mathrm{Pl} \to k$ a surjection inducing $A \to k$. Let $\ell$ be a prime different from $p$ and $k' \in \mathbb{N}$, and write $I_L$ for the set of $\sigma \in \mathrm{Pl}.\mathrm{inertiaSubgroupIn}\,\mathbb{Q}$ which fix $L$ pointwise. An element $\gamma \in I_L$ is given (`hγI`, `hγL`) such that (`hγ`) every $\tau \in I_L$ can be written $\tau = \gamma^{\,a} x^{\ell^{k'}} w^{\ell^{k'}}$ for some $a \in \mathbb{N}$ and $x, w \in I_L$. The displacement hypothesis `hdisp` asserts that for every $\sigma \in I_L$ and every $x$ in the $\ell^{k'}$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, \mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp))$ there are a $\mathrm{Pl}$-point $z$ of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ (over $\operatorname{Spec}\rho$) and $y \in J_{0s}$ with `gpts (σ • x - x)` equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{Pl}.\mathrm{subtype})$ followed by $z$, with `pts y` followed by the projection equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k)$ followed by $z$, and $\mathrm{proj}\,y = 0$. The invariance hypothesis `hfix` asserts conversely that for every $\sigma \in I_L$, every $\ell^{k'}$-torsion class $x$, and every such pair $(z, y)$ with `gpts x` equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{Pl}.\mathrm{subtype})$ followed by $z$, `pts y` followed by the projection equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k)$ followed by $z$ and $\mathrm{proj}\,y = 0$, one has $\sigma \cdot x = x$.
--
--   Conclusion. The cardinality of the $\ell^{k'}$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, \mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp))$ is at most the product of the cardinality of the image of the map $x \mapsto \gamma \cdot x - x$ on that torsion subgroup, viewed as a subset of $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp)$, and the cardinality of the set of $x \in \mathrm{JOne}(Mp)$ which lie in the $\ell^{k'}$-torsion subgroup and satisfy $\sigma \cdot x = x$ for every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $\mathrm{Pl}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ fixing $L$ pointwise.
--
--   This is the monodromy (displacement) count for the Jacobian of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$: given that all inertia displacements of $\ell^{k'}$-torsion classes are toric and that toric torsion classes are inertia-invariant, the $\ell^{k'}$-torsion is bounded by the image of $\gamma - 1$ times the inertia invariants. It feeds the subsequent step which produces, under the same orthogonality setting, toric representations of inertia displacements, on the route to level lowering at $p$.
